WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.360
Portrayed with affable charm by Jorge Garcia,
Hurley was the heart and soul of Lost, but

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:12.860
in his post-Lost life, the actor has kept
a relatively low profile despite working constantly.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.160
Here's a look at what he's been up to since
bidding farewell to the island.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.500
Following his star-making turn on Lost, Garcia
didn't waste much time booking his next gigs.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.200
It should come as no surprise that those gigs
came via his pal, Lost co-creator J.J. Abrams.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.200
First up was a brief, but hilariously memorable
turn as a bong-wielding security officer on

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.200
Abrams' under-appreciated sci-fi series Fringe.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.660
"And you're the best boss I've ever had."

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.820
Garcia followed that cameo with a much bigger
role on another Abrams series, the short-lived

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.380
crime drama Alcatraz.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:53.239
The show followed a young San Francisco detective
as she tried to unravel the mystery behind

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.060
the return of several long-deceased inmates
of the infamous island prison.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.500
Garcia played Dr. Diego Soto, a paranoid conspiracy
theorist who also happens to be an expert

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.120
on all things Alcatraz.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.760
Garcia's comedic chops have continued to land
him roles on television, including a couple

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.579
of episodes of one of the biggest sitcoms
of all time, How I Met Your Mother.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.619
He made his first appearance on the show in
2010 as Steve "The Blitz" Henry, an old college

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.920
friend of Marshall and Ted's.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.320
Much like Hurley, The Blitz appears to be
cursed with rotten luck, as he got his nickname

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.560
because he missed something amazing every
time he left a party early.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:32.520
The episode also makes clever use of Garcia's
Lost background by using his cursed lottery

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.920
numbers as a phone number.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.180
Garcia would reprise the role for another
brief but memorable cameo in the show's final

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.549
season, when we see that The Blitz's luck
hasn't changed all that much over the years.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:43.549
"Yes!

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:44.549
Whoo!"

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:47.100
"Aww, man!"

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:51.980
Unlike The Blitz, Garcia has had pretty good
luck in his own life, as he continues to book

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.640
notable supporting roles on popular TV shows.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.820
He even went back to his fantasy roots for
ABC's long-running fairy tale drama Once Upon

00:01:58.820 --> 00:01:59.420
a Time.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.480
Garcia appeared on three episodes of the show
between 2012 and 2013.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:08.900
In a case of pitch-perfect casting, he landed
the role of Anton, a magic bean-hoarding,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.420
surprisingly short giant with a fear of humans.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.900
"That's right, run!"

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.600
Unfortunately, though, Garcia didn't share
any screen time with his former Lost costar

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.220
Emilie de Ravin, who was a Once Upon a Time
regular as Belle.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:31.200
Garcia's most surprising cameo came in 2010,
when the actor's smiling face graced the cover

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.510
of Weezer's eighth album, the aptly titled
Hurley.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.989
Yes indeed, the album was actually named after
Garcia's beloved Lost character.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:43.540
As frontman Rivers Cuomo explained, after
deciding to use a photo of Garcia as the cover

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:47.390
art, the band realized that fans would just
"refer to it as 'the Hurley record.'"

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.300
So it only made sense to beat them to the
punch.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.920
Fortunately, the album didn't suffer its namesake's
generally rotten luck.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.400
It received a warm critical reception and
debuted at number six on the Billboard 200.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.760
In an even more surprising turn of events,
the band even invited Garcia to come perform

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.480
live with them on several tour stops supporting
the album, and honestly, he wasn't half bad.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.040
Garcia worked hard to make his fans laugh
when he appeared in 2015's The Ridiculous

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.550
Six, a Netflix original movie packed with
the likes of Adam Sandler, Rob Schneider,

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.530
and about a dozen or so other men and women.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.069
If you've never heard of Ridiculous Six, that's
probably because it wasn't very good.

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:24.900
In fact, it stands as one of the worst reviewed
films in Adam Sandler's career.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.200
That being said, Garcia's turn as the unintelligible
Herm was one of the few jokes that actually

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:30.700
worked.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.140
Although, considering the way the movie was
received, perhaps he'd rather forget he was

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.360
in the movie at all.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.060
"I just wish somebody here could speak Herm."

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:44.320
Since 2013, Garcia has portrayed local conspiracy
theorist-slash-consultant Jerry Ortega on

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.750
CBS' long-running Hawaii Five-O reboot.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.840
As it happens, it was the idea of a reunion
with his Lost costars Daniel Dae Kim and Terry

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.080
O'Quinn that led Garcia to take the role.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.740
The role was initially set as a two-episode
cameo, but Garcia was so good in the part

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.310
that producers quickly promoted him to series
regular.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:05.079
Now he has no plans on leaving the popular
series anytime soon.

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:09.230
That's no surprise, considering the perk of
shooting on the island paradise of Oahu, which

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.900
happens to be where the majority of Lost was
shot as well.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.719
While we're happy that Garcia has scored some
steady work, we're also a little worried that

00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:18.450
he's back on the island he worked so hard
to get away from.

